			},
			"date": "2023-04-14T23:07:23.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Adobe at some point created a VS Code extension that takes an exported CC Library from Adobe XD and converts it into a “Design System Package” (DSP: <a href=\"https://github.com/AdobeXD/design-system-package-dsp\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">github.com/AdobeXD/design-syst</span><span class=\"invisible\">em-package-dsp</span></a>) including design tokens as JSON. It even exports them into platform specific tokens via Style Dictionary (<a href=\"https://amzn.github.io/style-dictionary/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">amzn.github.io/style-dictionar</span><span class=\"invisible\">y/</span></a>). I demoed it in a few workshops for Adobe and really liked the approach. Unfortunately, it seems like development of the extension has been stopped. 😕</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
